{
  "_note": "Stock art for walk-on roles the GM might name in passing — a bartender, a beat cop — who are not part of the standing cast in cast-content.json and get no dossier of their own, just a face. Each entry also records how old the person looks and where the face is in the frame, so the interface can show the face rather than the whole scene. Looked up by features/cast/flavorArt.ts via `subject` (and optionally `gender` and `face`, the id of one variant: a subject and gender can have several, the original first, then a young and an older face; which one a place's person is comes from the campaign and the place, `pickFlavorFace`); `id` is the file's slug under public/images/flavor/, encoded at the same two WebP widths as cast art (tools/art/webp.mjs --widths=1024,512).",
  "_schema": {
    "id": "string — file slug under public/images/flavor/, no extension or width suffix",
    "type": "\"person\" for now — reserved for a future non-person tier of static flavor art",
    "subject": "string — stable kebab-case role slug a caller looks up by, shared across every gender variant of the same role",
    "gender": "\"male\" | \"female\"",
    "age": "number — how old the person in the picture looks. Read through engine/identity.ts ageBand() for the narrator, so the band is a fact of the picture rather than a thing the model guesses.",
    "face": "{x, y, size} — the square, in the 1024x683 source, that holds the head and shoulders. tools/art/flavor-faces.mjs cuts it to public/images/flavor/<id>-face.webp, the picture the interface shows beside a line of narration."
  },
